# SPIS — Solar Performance Improvement System

Research engine for a TUBITAK 2209-B project. Goal: quantify how environmental
soiling degrades PV performance at Canakkale Hybrid PP and turn that into a
data-driven, dynamic maintenance (panel-washing) schedule.

## Operating principles
- Every script must be reproducible: fixed seeds, explicit paths, no manual steps.
- Validate before you trust. After producing any number, re-derive it a second
  way (independent check) and assert they agree. Never report a metric you have
  not cross-checked.
- Prefer small, composable functions in `src/spis/` over notebook logic.
- Fail loud: raise on missing/unexpected data, never silently fillna without logging.

## Language & style
- All code, comments, docstrings, file names and commits in English.
- Write like a careful human engineer. No emoji anywhere. No phrases that reveal
  an AI author ("As an AI", "I cannot", "generated by"). No AI co-author trailers.

## Detailed rules load on demand
Methodology lives in `20-methodology.mdc`, Python standards in `10-python.mdc`,
git rules in `30-git.mdc`, data access in `40-data-access.mdc`. Read the matching
rule before working in its domain; do not restate it here.
